{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>It desires</b> — it stands firm. It has no parallel or cognate in Scripture. The commentators derive it from the root of חפץ, but I have no desire in it." "<b>Its terrors</b> — Targum: 'the terrors from beneath you,' and they are the testicles." "<b>They intertwine</b> — they become intertwined, from the root of שריגים; they become entangled."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The last phrase 'ואין לי בו חפץ' plays on the same root חפץ he is rejecting."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:27.753995690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}